  "scores": {
    "novelty": {
      "score": 2,
      "rationale": "The differentiation from 'Learning to Generate and Extract' (AAAI 2026, arXiv 2603.02909) is thin: that paper explicitly incorporates 'event structure constraints into the reward design' for zero-shot document-level event argument extraction on RAMS+WikiEvents — doing soft constraint enforcement during generation on the same benchmarks. Hard grammar vs. RL-soft-reward is an unvalidated design choice, not a fundamental scientific distinction. Critically, the proposal omits 'Adaptive Schema-aware Event Extraction with Retrieval-Augmented Generation' (ASEE, arXiv 2505.08690, May 2025), which directly addresses schema-aware event extraction by combining schema paraphrasing with RAG across 12 consolidated datasets in a new benchmark (MD-SEE). Grammar-constrained decoding via XGrammar/vLLM is also mature standard infrastructure, so the SCG module's contribution is largely engineering over a well-known tool."
