    "feasibility": {
      "score": 3,
      "rationale": "Core manual-mode experiments (~250h A100) translate to approximately 125–175 H100-equivalent hours, nominally under the 200 H100-hour hard limit; however, the auto mode at ~900h A100 (~450–630 H100-equiv) grossly violates the constraint and should not be presented as a valid mode. Qwen3-235B-A22B requires FP8 weights of ~235 GB, leaving <85 GB KV cache on 4×A100 80GB (320 GB total) — the vendor-recommended minimum is 8×H100; using 4×A100 forces INT4 quantization and severely limits batch throughput, undermining the quality of the generated training corpus."
